      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The present experiments have been performed in anesthetized dogs. They have allowed to determine the nocivity of air microembolus introduced directly in the circumflex branch of the left coronary artery. It has been suggested that to reduce post-operative disease due to microembolus at the end of an extracorporal circulation it is necessary to forbid the injection of isoprenalin and to realize a perfusion of papaverine."},
